<Base title="About GEAR" description="Learn the proposed mission, vision, values and founder-led governance approach of GEAR Moto Foundation.">
<section class="inner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Who We Are</div><h1>Driven by Riders.<br/><span class="accent">Built for Riders.</span></h1></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap prose"><h2>Our Mission</h2><p>GEAR Moto Foundation is being developed to strengthen the motorcycle community by expanding access to protective riding gear and education, promoting responsible road safety, connecting riders with practical guidance and services, and building need-based recovery support for motorcyclists and families facing serious motorcycle accidents.</p><h2>Our Vision</h2><p>A motorcycle community where safer riding is more accessible, riders look out for one another, and no rider facing a serious crash has to navigate the aftermath alone.</p><h2>Who We Serve</h2><p><strong>All Bikes. All Riders.</strong> We intend to serve an open-ended rider community, not a membership club, dealership, or fundraising vehicle for preselected individuals. Program assistance will be governed by charitable purpose, documented need and objective standards—not friendship, brand, sponsor, or club affiliation.</p><h2>Our Values</h2><ul><li><strong>Riders Helping Riders:</strong> Community connection paired with fair, objective charitable assistance.</li><li><strong>Safety Without Preaching:</strong> Equipment, skill and better decisions without shaming.</li><li><strong>Access:</strong> Lower barriers to protective equipment, education and recovery resources.</li><li><strong>Accountability:</strong> Sound stewardship, conflict safeguards and meaningful reporting.</li><li><strong>Keep Moving:</strong> Recovery supports stability and resilience without pressuring anyone to ride again.</li></ul><h2>Founder-Led. Board-Governed.</h2><p>Phillip “Wade” Gale is the founder and proposed President &amp; Executive Director. The draft operating model places day-to-day management with the executive leader and fiduciary oversight with an independent board. Final appointments and governance rights remain subject to incorporation, board action and legal review.</p><div class="program-callout"><strong>Organizational status:</strong> GEAR's formation, governing documents and charitable recognition must be verified before publication as completed facts. This page describes the current development plan.</div><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="/programs/">Explore Our Mission</a><a class="btn btn-outline-dark" href="/impact/">Transparency Approach</a></div></div></section></Base>